          "Picking random bit sizes or hash counts ruins Bloom efficiency: too few bits `m` saturates every bit to `1`, letting false positives climb toward 100%; too many hashes `k` burns CPU hashes AND fills up bits twice as fast, hurting accuracy!",
          "Classic information theory gives exact closed-form sizing equations for `n` expected keys per SSTable and desired target false-positive probability `p`:",
