          "Network latency, mobile disconnection, batching pauses, and out-of-order routing mean that event-time records frequently arrive minutes or hours late, out of sequence relative to other events.",
          "If a stream analytics window aggregates financial transactions using Processing Time, an accidental network hiccup shifts transactions across hour boundaries, corrupting revenue metrics and regulatory fraud reports.",
          "To process data by Event Time deterministically, stream engines require Watermarks: a watermark `W(t)` is a monotonically advancing timestamp emitted into the stream asserting: 'we do not expect any more events with timestamp `t' <= t`'.",
          "Analyze the formal time domain distinctions and watermark progression logic below.",
          "Understanding skew between Event Time and Processing Time is crucial during system upgrades or cold replays: when reprocessing historic data from cloud object storage, Processing Time advances at thousands of records per second while Event Time reflects the original timestamps from months prior.",
