          "Kyle Kingsbury's Knossos and Jepsen checkers optimize linearizability verification using the Wing & Gong algorithm (1993) combined with prune-and-search heuristics.",
          "The checker constructs a linearization point search tree: it attempts to place each concurrent operation at an instant between its invocation and completion timestamp such that the sequential execution matches the sequential specification of the data type (e.g. a register, set, or FIFO queue).",
